The '''2025 FA Community Shield''' was the 103rd [[FA Community Shield]], an annual [[association football]] match contested by the winners of the previous season's [[Premier League]] and [[FA Cup]] competitions. It was played at [[Wembley Stadium]] in London on 10 August 2025, and featured the [[2024–25 Premier League]] winners [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]] and the [[2024–25 FA Cup]] winners [[Crystal Palace F.C.|Crystal Palace]].

Crystal Palace beat Liverpool 3–2 on [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalties]] after a 2–2 draw on normal time, winning their first Community Shield title.

[[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] were the holders, having won the [[2024 FA Community Shield|2024 edition]], but they did not qualify for this match, being defeated in the [[2025 FA Cup final|FA Cup final]] and having finished third in the league.

==Background==
{{Main|2024–25 Crystal Palace F.C. season|2024–25 Liverpool F.C. season}}
[[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]] and [[Crystal Palace F.C.|Crystal Palace]] qualified for the 2025 FA Community Shield as the winners of the [[2024–25 Premier League]] and the [[2024–25 FA Cup]], respectively. It was the 67th meeting between the two sides, and the first appearance for Crystal Palace in a Community Shield match, after they earned their first ever major trophy in winning the FA Cup.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/live/cm23zrkn7ryt |title=Crystal Palace 1–0 Manchester City: Crystal Palace beat Man City to win FA Cup & end wait for major trophy|date=17 May 2025|work=BBC Sport|accessdate=17 May 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |first=Andy |last=Newton |title=When Is The 2025 Community Shield? As FA Cup Winners Crystal Palace Face League Champions Liverpool |url=https://www.sportscasting.com/uk/news/community-shield-2025-date-time-liverpool-crystal-palace/ |work=SportsCasting |date=18 May 2025 |accessdate=18 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250518113807/https://www.sportscasting.com/uk/news/community-shield-2025-date-time-liverpool-crystal-palace/ |archive-date=18 May 2025 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Liverpool have previously appeared in 24 Community Shield matches, winning 16 titles (sharing five of which), and appearing most recently in the [[2022 FA Community Shield|2022]] edition, where they beat Manchester City 3–1 at the [[King Power Stadium]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/61587053|title=Liverpool 3 Man City 1: Live|date=30 July 2022|work=BBC Sport|access-date=10 August 2022}}</ref>

==Match==

===Summary===
[[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]] took an early lead in the 4th minute when [[Hugo Ekitike]] scored with a low shot into the right corner. [[Crystal Palace F.C.|Crystal Palace]] equalised in the 17th minute through a [[Jean-Philippe Mateta]] penalty into the right of the net, awarded after a foul in the box by [[Virgil van Dijk]] on [[Ismaïla Sarr]]. [[Jeremie Frimpong]] restored Liverpool's advantage in the 21st minute with a cross-shot from the right that looped into the net after hitting the far post. Crystal Palace levelled again in the 77th minute when Ismaïla Sarr converted from the right, in-off the post, after an incisive through-ball.<ref>{{cite web | last1=Aarons | first1=Ed | title=Crystal Palace sink Liverpool on penalties to claim Community Shield | work=The Guardian | url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2025/aug/10/crystal-palace-liverpool-community-shield-match-report }}</ref>

With the score tied 2–2 at full time, the match went to a penalty shoot-out. Crystal Palace goalkeeper [[Dean Henderson]] saved from [[Alexis Mac Allister]] and [[Harvey Elliott]], after [[Mohamed Salah]] had missed the target with a shot over the bar. [[Justin Devenny]] converted the winning penalty to the right of the net as Crystal Palace triumphed 3–2 in the shoot-out, securing their first-ever Community Shield title in their inaugural appearance in the fixture.<ref>{{cite web |last=Athletic |first=The |date=10 August 2025 |title=Crystal Palace beat Liverpool on penalties to win Community Shield: Live updates and reaction |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/live-blogs/crystal-palace-vs-liverpool-live-updates-score-result/q4h3pYHFn4UE/ |access-date=10 August 2025 |website=The Athletic}}</ref>

